docs {
  # Notifications

  Provides user notification inbox management, High-Water Mark read tracking, reconnect catch-up sync, and group owner manual announcements.

  ## Endpoints

  | Method | Path | Action |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `GET` | `/api/v1/notifications` | Get cursor-paginated notifications timeline |
  | `GET` | `/api/v1/notifications/unread-count` | Get lightweight unread badge counter |
  | `GET` | `/api/v1/notifications/sync` | Catch up missed notifications since last received ID |
  | `GET` | `/api/v1/notifications/:id` | Get details of a single notification |
  | `POST` | `/api/v1/notifications/read` | Mark all or up to a specific notification as read |
  | `POST` | `/api/v1/notifications/:id/read` | Mark a specific single notification as read |
  | `DELETE` | `/api/v1/notifications/:id` | Soft-delete a single notification |
  | `DELETE` | `/api/v1/notifications` | Clear all or only read notifications from inbox |
  | `POST` | `/api/v1/groups/:groupID/announcements` | Group owner manual broadcast announcement |
}
